# CVE-2024-23342 (GHSA-wj6h-64fc-37mp / PYSEC-2026-1325)
# Minerva timing attack on the P-256 curve in python-ecdsa.
#
# python-ecdsa is pulled in transitively by python-jose. Upstream
# (tlsfuzzer/python-ecdsa) states side-channel attacks are out of scope
# for the project and there is NO planned fix, so no version bump can
# clear this finding.
#
# Not reachable in this application: docker-compose.yml sets
# JWT_ALGORITHM=HS256 and no ES256 keypair is configured, so python-jose
# never touches the ecdsa code path (ecdsa is only used for the ES*
# algorithms). The advisory also states signature VERIFICATION is
# unaffected; only nonce-leaking signing would be exposed.
#
# Accepted risk. Revisit when python-jose drops the ecdsa dependency or
# when ES256 signing is ever enabled.
CVE-2024-23342

# CVE-2026-85394 (GHSA-6c5p-j8vq-pqhj)
# python-jose accepts a DER-encoded public key as an HMAC secret, so a
# client holding the server's public key can forge HS256 tokens when
# jwt.decode() is called WITHOUT an explicit `algorithms` allowlist.
#
# No patched version exists: python-jose 3.5.0 is the latest release
# and the advisory lists no fixed version, so no version bump can
# clear this finding (Snyk: "There is no fixed version").
#
# Not reachable in this application: the only decode path is
# jwt_service.decode_token, which pins algorithms=[self.algorithm]
# (HS256 with SECRET_KEY, or ES256 with the configured public PEM).
# No call feeds raw DER bytes to decode, and the advisory states that
# an explicit allowlist excluding HS256 rejects the forgery before the
# key is examined.
#
# Accepted risk. Revisit if a patched python-jose ships, or if a
# jwt.decode() call is ever added without an explicit algorithms list.
CVE-2026-85394
